For reference, I've never tried to use gnuwin's make/gcc/etc.  I've
always used mingw.

> In file included from ../src/monst.c:5:
> ../include/config.h:191:1: warning: "DLB" redefined

My suspicion is that config.h has gotten messed up slightly in the patch
process.  Check and make sure all the options are sane; also be sure that
anything that uses regex (menucolors, statuscolors) is turned off,
unless you have the regex libraries available -- the below errors look
like you don't.

> In file included from ../src/monst.c:22:
> ../include/color.h:10:21: regex.h: No such file or directory
> In file included from ../src/monst.c:22:
> ../include/color.h:64: error: field `match' has incomplete type
> make: *** [o/monst.o] Error 1

Both of these indicate that regex headers (and libraries) are likely
missing.  If you comment out the line reading:

#define MENU_COLOR_REGEX

then you may have better luck.

